Triumph of the populist right in Austria, together they form 29%
Early elections to the Austrian parliament have brought according to the first approximate results, an appreciable weakening of both parties of the current grand coalition and an expressive strengthening of the populist right party.
Some strong and special losses have suffered the Austrian Popular Party (OVP), where the position of the current president, Wilhelm Molterer, is seriously wobbling.
By contrast, the leader of the Alliance for the future of Austria (BZO), the head of the Carinthian state government, Jörg Haider, prepares his triumphant return to national politics.
According to approximate results, social democracy (SPÖ) remains the strongest party in the country with 29.8 percent of votes, losing a 5.5 percent vote compared to the last elections in 2006.
Worst the OVP has yet lost 25.6 percent, nearly nine percent vote.
They are the worst results, literally catastrophic, in the history of these two great Austrian parties from the post-war and especially for the people who called these early elections.
Still in early July, when the OVP left the coalition, the popular had in terms of preference against the SPO, a considerable advantage.
It’s clear, however, that voters punished them for letting the government shipwreck.
Already in the first reactions to the results, speculation was heard about the resignation of the president of the party and, until today, vice chancellor, Wilhelm Molterer.
Observers believe that it could already arrive on Monday at the exceptional meeting of the presidency of the party.
Such an evolution would obviously facilitate the path of the constant and closest starting point of the electoral results, that is, of the renewal of the grand coalition between SPO and OVP.
In view of the fact that the reinforcement of both parties of the populist right – the liberals (FPOs) have won approximately 18 percent and the BZO, eleven percent of the votes – and that the Social Democrats at the same time expressed their fears that the same would be repeated in 1999 when the people negotiated with the populists (then FPO was a unity, but in 2005 they dismantled from BZO)
Because of this evolution, Haider clearly bets who already announced that he is prepared to collaborate with any party and that he already assumes his return to Vienna, to national politics.
Also the Green Party has managed to reach parliament although it has lost slightly and descended from third to fifth place among the Austrian political parties.
No other party clearly exceeded the four percent limit and is therefore not part of parliament.
Schwarzenbeng: relations with India can cool
If it is not possible to solve the problem of the Czech scientists who have been accused in India for illegally collecting beetles it could lead to a cooling of Czech-Indian relations, according to Foreign Minister Karel Schwarzenberg.
This is how the minister said in New York, after today’s meeting with his Indian counterpart, Pranab Mukherjee.
"If this were not fixed then yes, then it would surely arrive at this cooling," he said after the meeting that was organized on a Czech initiative.
Mukherjee said, after the meeting, that in legal matters the executive can hardly get involved.
However, he said that in the case of Petr Švácha, who was exempt from prosecution and punished with a fine, the government can negotiate with the local government of Darjiling in whose jurisdiction the matter falls.
"Their problem could be solved," the minister said.
For Emil Kučera, sentenced to three years in prison it would be best, according to Mukherjee, to appeal to the highest instances.
You can then apply for exoneration of the case and wait the sentencing free, he explained.
Schwarzenbeng confirmed that his colleague expressed himself on the same terms during the meeting.
"He advises to appeal to the High Court and then it would be possible to pardon," the head of Czech diplomacy said.
The only way the Czech side can get into the matter is to get the convict a "legal competent support," the Indian minister said.
On the other hand, he said that such support has already been achieved by the Indian side.
“We have the greatest interest in maintaining with India the best relations, which have a long tradition.
The Indians also recognize it," Schwarzenberg said.
On the other hand, as the ČTK said before his colleague he insisted that the Czech Republic considers the problem of Czech entomologists of great importance.
"We really think it's a tremendous mistake to imprison and condemn these Czech scientists," he said.
The minister circumvented the answer to the question of whether he received from the Indian side the promise that he would deal with the matter.
“I’ve received quite a few promises,” he only found.
Czech arbitrates a fight on the seafloor
I approach an electronic wall map, it depicts Australia surrounded by sea.
He is not interested, however, by the mainland but by a small point lost in the blue ocean.
"The island belongs to Australia and next to it also the seafloor that surrounds it.
“The region is, at the same time, as large as a single continent,” says Italian lawyer Luigi Santouosso, who belongs to the thirty-member team working in the U.N. Division for Ocean and Sea Law Affairs.
Its boss, director of the Division, Czech lawyer Václav Mikulka, follows the exposure and sometimes completes it.
Govern this mood and enthusiasm of work.
The seafloor hides to this day a little-known world, rich in natural sources.
Oil and other mineral raw materials can be found, but also unknown organisms until today that themselves carry the key to the development of anti-cancer drugs.
The bottom is greater than the mainland
The countries with the coast have begun today to vehemently contest the new territories under the sea.
According to the U.N
It is mainly the so-called mainland Edge which sometimes extends a few hundred kilometers from the coast of the given country.
It has, according to the Treaty, exclusive rights in all the resources of the mainland Edge.
"Simplically, by mainland Edge is meant the part of the seabed and its surface, which is a natural continuation of the continent underwater.
It reaches the edge of the sea coast, and often, to the border of the two hundred marine miles, i.e. pure economic zone," Mikulka explains.
The request that the given country submits to the Commission, for the delimitation of the outer limits of the Edge continent, must be delivered with scientific technical documentation based on research and measures.
It is the result of a series of years of job preparation.
“One of our tasks is to organize a technical and legal specialist aid commission.
The commission has filed five requests from Russia, Brazil, Australia, Ireland and New Zealand.
For now, only those of the last three aforementioned countries have come forward," Mikulka adds.
Not long ago, Australia’s success had a worldwide repercussion as it was the first to essentially expand its marine dominance.
However, New Zealand also succeeded - the seafloor surface granted by the commission last week is 1.6 million square kilometers, that is, almost six times more than the size of the state itself.
Both countries invested millions of pains for their study.
The gain that will arise from the use of the seafloor will be, as they promise, invaluable.
Other states are also slowly submitting their applications.
They can carry it out until ten years from the moment they ratified the "Treaty of Montego Bay".
Where the mainland ends begins the region of the ocean floor declared by Treaty as "common heritage of humanity".
Already here, none nation has an exclusive position.
The right of exploitation in these areas is administered by the Treaties established by international institutions.
"The seabed, however, is no gold mine," director Mikulka says with emphasis, adding "that its separate areas are legally and clearly restricted and its regime defined by contract."
Czech in the Pacific
And today, part of the seabed also belongs to the Czech Republic.
It is distributed with other countries of the then Eastern Bloc within the common organization "Interoceanmetal".
This was achieved in 1991 with a treaty as investors the same as a few other states, states called "the pioneering investor".
It is empowered to explode in the ClarionClipperton area in the Pacific Ocean, between Mexico, the Hawaii Islands and Kiribati.
The area to be researched by the investor is somewhat larger than the old Czechoslovakia.
The bottom there is bumpy, it's about something like a tatra marine aftershock.
"An area can be exploited of a total area of 75,000 square kilometres.
The area is rich in polymetallic concretion deposits containing nickel, copper, cobalt and manganese, "adds Indian lawyer Pakshi Rajan.
A Macedonian employee of the Division, Rober Sandev, brings us a sample of that kind of concretion.
It reminds us of a small potato or with a little fantasy, the Shem, which according to legend revived the Golem.
During the release of the hostages the German special forces command was at the place of action
To solve the hostage crisis the government of Egypt had asked for Germany’s help – experts came.
When the situation became serious, the special forces command was ready, but the operation was not carried out.
More and more details are known about the circumstances of the liberation of 11 European tourists in Egypt.
