The first chamber of the United States Congress soon failed with a large salvation package of 700 billion dollars for the financial markets.
The Dow Jones fell very drastically.
The U.S
Despite all appeals from President George W. Bush and former politicians from both parties he did not reach a majority for the program with which disorder in financial markets should be limited.
