Organizers register the increase in the number of reservations
It seems to be a good winter for German travel organizers:
According to a study, the sales volume of travel reservations for the coming months increased compared to last year – even the winter season by more than 30 percent.
According to a study, despite the weakened juncture the desire to travel of the Germans remains as before.
As the German travel association (DVR) reported on Monday in Berlin, with travel reservations for the winter season travel agencies recorded a sales volume that is 31 percent more compared to the same period last year.
According to GfK’s market research institute’s research institute, reserves for the fall months had already risen in number.
Thus the sales volume of travel agencies in October was almost eleven percent more compared to 2007, the DVR reported.
The basis of the results are GfK figures that are the information analyzed about the reservations in 1200 travel agencies and computed approximately for the entire market.
The data collected are the travel reservations made until the end of August 2008.
Due to the weakened course of the dollar especially travel to the United States is in high demand, the DRV reported.
In this case the number of reservations increased to almost a third.
The preferred destination points of the Germans are not only Spain, Turkey and Greece but also the regions of Germany.
Above all, organized trips are very preferred, explains Klaus Laepple, the president of DRV.
In view of the fact that energy and food prices increase, in this case travel expenses are "better calculable for the customer than during an individual trip".
Among other things consumers can save money with early booking discounts or All-Inclusive offers, Laepple explained.
Also in the summer months the trips were well reserved, so that the volume of sales compared to last year again rose – although according to another study the number of Germans making a trip, comparing last year, fell.
My first Oktoberfest
