Morgan Stanley sells stake to Japanese MUFG
Morgan Stanley announced the entry into its capital of Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group (MUFG), the first Japanese bank, which will disburse nine billion dollars to acquire 21% of its capital, a news that has been accepted with a sharp decrease in its listing.
A week after discovering a provisional agreement, both banks explained that MUFG was going to buy 9.9% of the Morgan Stanley common shares at the price per unit of 25.25 dollars, i.e. an amount of three billion dollars.
The agreed price is less than 19 % of the share’s book value as at 31 August.
MUFG will invest six billion additional dollars with the purchase of convertible securities which will insure a return of 10% and a conversion price of 31.25 dollars.
Morgan Stanley specified that the overall operation would be carried out based on a price per unit of measure of 29 dollars, that is 28% above its current change.
The Morgan Stanley share lost 6,79% to US$23.07 each at 17:00 GMT.
“This strategic alliance is an important opportunity to accelerate Morgan Stanley’s transition to banking holding status,” explained Juan Mack, the American group’s CEO.
Morgan Stanley adopted this new statute last week, which would have to allow him to diversify his activities but he passes under the authority of the Federal Reserve.
Their alliance with MUFG also confirms that the current financial crisis forces Wall Street’s biggest names to adopt much more prudent behavior than before.
The modalities presented last Monday also show that the agreement has been modified in recent days: last Monday, Morgan had announced that it would sell up to 20% of its shares to Japanese for almost 8.5 billion dollars.
"A week ago, Toshihide Mizuno, MUFG's chief executive, explained in Tokyo, " we thought that participation would have been made up only of ordinary shares.
But in view of the current situation of the economy and the market, we have wished to minimize the risks and cover ourselves.”
Based on the weighted average price, MUFG will pay its Morgan Stanley securities 7% below its accounting value.
And the operation will be translated by a dilution of about 20% of the profit per share.
The agreement provides that MUFG may convert within one year half of its preferred securities into common shares if they are solded more than 50 % above the conversion price, i.e
Morgan Stanley assures that MUFG’s capitals will allow it to pick up investment opportunities, bolster its balance sheet and increase its liquidity.
A spokeswoman for the group nevertheless refused to give clarifications on the strategic projects of the two new allies.
After MUFG’s investment, Morgan Stanley should show a Tier One solvency ratio of about 15%, one of the best in the industry.
Morgan claimed to have greatly alleviated his balance since the end of August.
The last few weeks were tiring for the group, which saw its listing fall by half while the cost of security against a risk of defects on its debt took off.
This cost fell last Monday but remained at a high level, around 12%.
Last week, Goldman Sachs, the only other “survivor” of Wall Street’s large investment banks after the bankruptcies of Bear Stearns and Lehman Brothers and the purchase of Merrill Lynch, announced that it raised US$15 billion, in part for Berkshire Hathaway, Warren Buffett.
Rafael Correa in Quito on Monday.
Refounding the republic around 21st century socialism.
This is the common project of the Venezuelan Hugo Chavez, the Boliviano Evo Morales and the Ecuadorian Rafael Correa.
This Sunday, by way of his colleagues and friends, it is the third that put to the vote a project for a new Constitution.
Mission fulfilled since 64% of voters voted "yes" to the referendum, according to official results referring to 80 % of votes.
According to these results, the "no" obtained 28%, 7% of the votes were null votes and 0.7 % were blank votes.
In order for the draft Constitution to be adopted, it had to obtain half of the suffrages plus one.
On Sunday, two polls carried out at the exit of the polling stations and a recount by a non-governmental organization had announced a broad "yes" victory, estimating it between 63% and 70%.
Rafael Correa had also vindicated the victory of his draft Constitution on Sunday night to Monday.
The "Constitution triumphed overwhelmingly", he had assured, congratulating the Ecuadorians who head the government of Guayaquil, 280 kilometers southwest of Quito.
Thus, Rafael Correa has been congratulated by Chávez and Morales but also on their Chilean colleague Micaela Bachelet.
The elections, which will take place in full calm, according to the observation mission of the Organization of American States (OAS), referred to a 444-point text that consolidated the " new socialism " defended by the president.
The draft Constitution implies the increase of the power of the State over the economy, reserving the " development planning " of a country that lives essentially thanks to the extraction of oil by foreign companies and thanks to currencies sent by their emigrants.
Carried by Correa, elected in 2006, the project also grants reinforced powers to the head of state, who will be able to do up to two consecutive terms of four years each and will have the possibility of dissolving the Assembly.
Correa already announced that he would use this power and would want a new term in February 2009.
The Constitution also consolidates the principle of the free health and education services that the president began to establish 13.9 million inhabitants in this country, in which 50% of the population lives below the poverty line.
It finally foresees the interdiction of the presence of foreign troops, which will end the agreement between Quito and Washington for the use of an Ecuadorian base as a starting point for American anti-drug operations.
All 19 people kidnapped have been liberated in Chad
An Egyptian commando launched the assault on the raptors of the eleven tourists and their eight companions captured ten days ago.
They are in Cairo.
The eleven European tourists and their eight Egyptian companions kidnapped ten days ago in the desert arrived unharmed in the Egyptian capital after being released Monday afternoon.
In the morning, they had been liberated by Egyptian special forces in Chad.
All of them looked good upon arrival at 15H30 aboard a special aircraft to the Al Maza military base, adjacent to Cairo International Airport.
Helicopters immediately transported them to Maadi hospital, a residential suburb of Cairo, for medical testing, so they have not been able to talk to the press.
"They are in good health" and "no ransom was paid" to the hijackers, Egyptian Tourism Minister Zoheir Garana said at the airport.
On 19 September these hostages fell in the possession of 35 unknown kidnappers while enjoying an off-road safari in a desert area at the foot of Mount Ouanat, on the ends of Egypt, Sudan and Libya, and have since gone from one zulo to another.
The group consisted of eleven tourists – five Italians, five Germans and one Romanian – and eight Egyptians: two guides, four drivers, a border guard and the director of the Aegyptous travel agency, in charge of the safari organization.
An Egyptian security official said that 30 members of the special forces, transported aboard two helicopters, had launched the assault during the night before dawn.
"An exchange of gunfire occurred, killing half of the kidnappers, the others have fled," said this official who kept the anonymous.
According to him, 150 members of the Egyptian special forces of the "lightning" unit were sent to Sudan, where they had the support of German and Italian commandos.
Italian Foreign Minister Franco Frattini mentioned in Belgrade the role played by secret agents and members of the Italian special forces.
"It must be recognized that we have achieved this result thanks to the professionalism and effectiveness of our men of the secret services, of the special forces," he said without elaborating.
He also denied paying a ransom.
On the eve of the Sudanese army claimed to have intercepted during an all-terrain patrol aboard which the kidnappers were located, of which they killed six, including the Chadian chief and arrested two.
He also stated that they were related to a rebellious group in Darfur, the Sudan-Unity Liberation Movement (SLA-U), an assertion immediately denied by this group.
Letras - Silent majority of culture
A debate on the financing of fait les manchette culture and occupies the current electoral campaign.
Better like that.
But a sector of our cultural life remains forever forgotten.
Which will arise to denounce the miserable sums granted to small museums, archives, archaeological excavations or starving national historical sites?
Which politician will dare to remind the federal government to neglect its monuments and heritage buildings?
Why don’t we have true laws that effectively preserve our heritage as in Canada and Quebec?
Did you know that the French government devotes three and a half million euros to restoring only the castle of Chinon in the Loire valley?
In the United States, it is written in its Constitution that the protection of heritage is part of the culture of Americans and that this heritage has to be protected by all citizens, all elect and all government departments, and all of this, in consultation.
In Quebec, in the Federation of Quebec History Societies, at least 40 000 benevolent people regrouped into 211 societies of history, heritage, archives and genealogy are concerned to seek in history, preserve with little money piles of private archives and preserve archaeological vestiges.
These are often the watchdogs of our heritage, who protest with energy and despair when promoters and perpetrators throw their bulldozers against our old stones and our forgotten cemeteries.
By when, a memorial for history and heritage?
The governments of the Netherlands nationalize a part of Fortis Bank.
The States of the Netherlands - being the first in Europe - will help with a nationalization the Belgian-Dutch bank Fortis that is in distress due to the effect of the mortgage crisis of the North American market: the three countries will support in total with 11.2 billion euros to this financial and insurance institution that also has business in Hungary.
This weekend the governments of Belgium, Luxembourg and the Netherlands held higher-level consultations with the president of the European Central Bank and responsible for the economic competition of the European Commission.
Fortis Bank is the first that suffered the Eurozone crisis within the framework of the international financial crisis that has been taking place in several waves more than a year ago, therefore the decisions taken with regard to the Bank, in a sense they can be considered as precedents.
According to the decision taken in the early hours of Sunday, the three states will buy about half (49 percent) of the property owned by the Bank in their area.
The Bank will surely sell a part of its businesses, including above all the activities -mainly insurance- bought last year of the Dutch ABN Amró.
Fortis actions began a sharp decline last week and for the second half of the week there were already significant signs of crisis in the institution.
However, analysts agree in pointing out that with its 85 thousand employees this Bank is too large to allow it to break.
The company’s shares on Friday alone declined by 12 percent, this being the lowest point in the last 14 years.
Since January the value of stocks declined with more than two-thirds.
Looking at current stock prices, the total value of the group’s capital in the market is around 14 billion euros, but according to the company’s executives this is not real.
The Bank’s management charged the sharp decline in Fortis stocks with U.S. market insecurities in relation to the approval of the 700 billion-dollar U.S. package plan.
On Monday, stocks already showed a slight increase.
On Friday Filip Dierckx was appointed as the bank’s new CEO.
The Bank also looked for private investors, but so far no one has given a concrete offer.
The Belgian government had previously assured that investors didn’t have to worry, they won’t lose their money.
Among the Bank’s clients so far there was no panic, they did not invade the bank offices to withdraw their money.
Fortis has its own branch in Hungary and has also bought leasing companies.
Zorro in the chicken coop
In the U.S., living and health insurance companies by looking at drug purchase data often denies signing an insurance contract.
Specialists in the privacy policy fear that the personal data market will become uncontrollable.
"There are personal data protection programs, which to the use of prescription data in all cases binds you to the approval of the given person.
It must be in independent hands, because if not, "we entrust the fox chicken coop" - quotes the Washington Post to Richard Dick, designer of the prescription follow-up program.
Insurance companies depend on the price of insurance and the amount of compensation of the client’s health status and if they believe that the risk is excessive, they simply don’t make the contract.
Previously they sent the client to medical control and signed with him the contract already knowing the result of the control.
Dick ten years ago invented a much cheaper procedure: with the client’s identification number he easily gets from pharmacies the list of medicines purchased in the last year and a half and the program itself draws the conclusion on the client’s diseases and health status.
For example, if you systematically take large doses of cholesterol-lowering pills, it indicates that the level of fat in the blood is virtually incurably high, so you are immediately included in a higher risk category.
Numerous versions of the program circulate, some even establish a risk number, so the insurance company in addition to the administration barely has something to do, although there are small difficulties in this regard.
Among the disadvantages of the program is for example that some medications are multipurpose, for example certain substances serve both to treat the headache and heat waves and even as antidepressants.
The latter is an important risk-increasing factor for insurance companies while the former are not.
Special companies were constituted to consult and process this data, which before acquiring the necessary information from the pharmacies, ask for the approval of the patient.
The authorities already force them to this, although they did not receive a fine for the negligence so far.
Some companies lately also elaborate the results of the laboratory tests and joining them with the drug consumption data get more accurate information about the patient’s health status.
More and more companies have access to this data and simultaneously it is increasingly difficult to control its use.
There is an exclusive law for the protection of personal health data, but it applies only to insurance companies and those that provide health services.
Already before Congress is the bill that provides the right to the authority for the control of specialized companies for the provision of personal data.
Dick Richard acknowledges that this is insufficient: he therefore developed his program, which will require the specific approval of the person for the provision of their own personal data.
It is another issue that that person cannot deny their approval, because otherwise the insurance companies will not sign the contract with him.
So the chickens, despite everything, are exposed to the goodwill of the fox.
Marsella Global Menu
The European Union doubles its trade with India
As the European Union and India are reciprocally trading partners, this issue in addition to the other mostly global problems dominated the agenda of the ninth summit.
There will also be a Franco-Indian summit today, mainly to discuss cooperation in nuclear energy.
Although the European Union recognizes that India is a great developing democratic power that should have more voice and vote in international affairs but member countries have not yet been able to reach a common denominator on whether they should support New Delhi as a permanent member of the UN Security Council.
This issue has not been dealt with at the 9th summit started yesterday in Marseille.
French President Nicolas Sarkozy, President-in-Office of the EU, José Manuel Barroso president of the Commission and Javier Solana main representative of foreign policy, received Manmohan Singh, Prime Minister of India with which they reached an agreement to double in five years, i.e
Bearing in view that between 2000 and 2007 the exchange of goods increased from 25 billion to 55 billion, this is not an overly ambitious objective.
This legally harmonized the twenty-six existing bilateral civil aviation conventions with India, so air transport may also fly in the future.
India until the end of 2009 wants to sign the free trade agreement with the Union.
Sarkozy vowed to expedite negotiations.
The goal is balance, because while the EU is India’s first trading partner, New Delhi is only in the 9th place among the Union’s trading partners.
The summit paid attention to global issues.
Both sides condemned the Afghan and Pakistani situation and terrorism - all forms of the latter - and urged the convening of a UN conference.
The conclusion of the Doha round of trade liberalization was also encouraged, although both sides have great responsibility for their failure.
The EU confirmed that it will cling to its energy and climate programme, that is, until 2020 it wants to reduce polluting emissions by at least twenty percent.
India also agrees with this, just as in next year’s climate conference a global agreement should be reached and greenhouse gas production decreased to 2050.
They also want to hamper the rise in food prices and supported the convening of an international conference to review the financial crisis.
Today the head of government of India will travel to the French capital, where - in a bilateral meeting - he will sign an agreement on the peaceful use of nuclear energy.
Paris is confident that the French companies will receive commissions worth twenty billion euros to build nuclear reactors.
According to news agency reports the agreement would be for a period of 15 years.
In Frankfurt more than three hundred Italian publishers
Strong presence of Italian publishers to the international exhibition of the Frankfurt book.
More than three hundred Italian publishers present at the 60th edition of the Buchmesse, the most important international meeting for the exchange of rights.
The international exhibition of the Frankfurt book awaits for this edition more than 7 thousand exhibitors from 102 different countries that will occupy the 171,790 square meters of the exhibition with more than 403 thousand titles in exhibition and with Turkey as a guest of honor.
It will be the undersecretary of the Ministry of goods and cultural activities Francisco Maria Giro to represent the Italian government in the opening ceremony of the Italian pavilion: Italy will be institutionally and effectively present with a point Italy - 264 square meters of exhibition space.
There will be an encounter with the picture in the Room Struktur in Hall 5.0 of the Buchmesse: this will be the occasion to present numbers, trends and prospects on the status of publishers in Italy.
According to the data, the weight of the books of foreign authors progressively decreases over the total of Italian production, and in particular that for adults and adolescents.
Steve Fossett's plane found missing millionaire a year ago
The wreckage of Steve Fossett’s plane, the millionaire missing on September 3, 2007 while flying over the Nevada desert, has been found.
Debris has been found over a 3000-meter-altitude plateau in the area of Mammoth Lakes’ Nevada mountain range at the California-Nevadia site.
Inside the plane, there were no human remains.
Madera County commissioner John Anderson has dispelled the remaining doubts: "The plane has been located, we have sent a squad, and now we have the confirmation that it is typical of what Steve Fossett was flying on the day of his disappearance," he said in a print conference.
The commissioner has specified that no human remains have been found either on the plane or in the surroundings.
The 63-year-old has been killed in February.
The U.S. Transportation Safety (Ntsb) office has made it known that a few hours after sightinging of the wreckages has been sent by an investigator that has identified the apparatus: it’s typical of the Bellanca 8kcab, scattered since September 3, 2007, when Fossett took off from Yerington in Nevada for a three-hour flight.
Yesterday, always in California, not far away with the confine of Nevada, some Fossett’s personal remains have been found by a couple near their Mammoth Lakes home.
These are two documents called Fossett, the two issued by the Federal Aviation Administration of the Illinois, cash and a sweatshirt.
Fossett's search had been interrupted a month after his disappearance.
The millionaire had become a place in history thanks to a long series of scoops.
In 2002, to the sixth attempt, he had become the first Man to complete the turn of the world in a hot air balloon: two solitary weeks of flight.
Three years later he had made the turn of the world by plane and nonstop.
Among his record, also that for having flowned at 15,445 meters high, over the Andes, but with a co-driver.
Glk, the advertising you don't expect
A Suv outside the schemes with an original and well-established design with defined lines and certain angles.
It is this, in short, Glk the last born among the "compacted" all-terrain vans of the house of the star with which Mercedes-Benz has sought to give a novelty window in this sector.
Proper for the content outside the traditional, it will be unexpected and unconventional, the communication that will accompany the launch of the suv Glk, available in Mercedes-Benz exhibition halls from next October 17.
The advertising campaign that will accompany the debut of the new car launched an unpublished form of communication through a 3D advertising campaign, used for the first time in Italy by an automobile brand.
A project with maxi-posters, articulated in three different phases, that dominated the central street of the Milanese shopping, Avenida Como, until November 15.
The first phase of this new type of communication will begin with the presentation of the car in stereoscopic version and thanks to special glasses distributed in the avenue How it will be possible to see the new suv in almost real dimensions and in three-dimensional format.
Indeed, looking at the images you will have the impression that the car leaves the poster.
Successively, through the use of the innovative Elumina8 technology the new Glk will be illuminated at different times in all its details, to recompose in a single image.
Undoubted Mercedes with this advertising is trying to introduce something new in the stereotype of automotive communication.
Will you be able with this formula to capture the interest of future buyers? we will see.
